{
  "configuration_id": "config_034",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_025: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile; acc=0.725) has been validated across RNA encoder (scvi_n200 >> pca_n2000 > scgpt) and aggregation (transformer > avgpool) choices. However, the image encoder effect has never been isolated in the multiprofile setting—all completed multiprofile experiments use imagenet_vit_l. Config_034 changes only the image encoder to resnet50 while keeping scvi_n200, transformer, weighted, and multiprofile fixed, providing a clean single-variable comparison against config_025. This is the highest-value next experiment because: (1) it resolves the largest remaining uncertainty about a core design axis, (2) if resnet50 is competitive it broadens the feasible design space, and (3) if it underperforms significantly it confirms imagenet_vit_l as a necessary component, preventing wasted budget on resnet50-based variants. No other single experiment reduces as much uncertainty about the optimal architecture under the limited budget."
}

